{% set local_problem %}
<p>Some Cullman properties face drainage challenges that surface solutions can't fully address. Lots that slope toward the house, areas with high water tables, or properties where surface extensions would cross walkways, patios, or established landscaping all benefit from underground drainage.</p>

<p>For homeowners who maintain meticulous landscaping — and Cullman has many — underground drains offer another advantage: no visible extensions, splash blocks, or hoses interrupting carefully designed outdoor spaces. Water simply disappears underground and emerges far from the home.</p>

<p>Properties around Smith Lake may face additional challenges with humidity and elevated water tables. Underground drains can be essential for protecting foundations in these environments.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water through sealed channels to a discharge point far from your foundation. The system works entirely by gravity — no pumps, no electricity, no moving parts.</p>

<p>We use 4-inch PVC or corrugated pipe buried 8-12 inches deep, with proper slope (typically 1-2% grade) ensuring water flows continuously to the exit point. Pop-up emitters or daylight exits release water where it can safely disperse.</p>

<p>The result is complete water management that functions automatically, invisibly, and indefinitely.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage systems throughout Cullman County for over 20 years. We design systems that solve problems permanently, use quality materials that last, and take care to minimize disruption to your property.</p>

<p>We'll assess your situation honestly. If simpler solutions will work, we'll say so. If underground drains are the right choice, we'll explain why and design a system that meets your specific needs.</p>
{% endset %}
